  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday morning through next Wednesday)\nIssued at 214 PM EDT Thu Sep 17 2026\n\nThe ridge is finally expected to break down Sunday into Monday as a \nfront approaches. Isolated thunderstorms will be possible on Sunday \nafternoon, becoming more widespread on Monday but total rainfall is \nexpected to be less than an inch for much of the CWA through the \nforecast period. \n\nThe front will bring afternoon thunderstorms back into the forecast \nto start off next week. This will help to moderate temps down to the \nupper 80s and low 90s. There are some signs that temps will drop \ninto the low 80s towards the end of next week as more dry air clears \nout afternoon convection chances.",
